  "boundaries": {
    "generic_dispatch": "Once a constructed record carrying a vtable base leaves its constructor, later reads of the method entry go through that record's vtable field generically (a load of the field at +0x18 for the header form, or at +0x0 for the slot-base form); those dispatch sites are shared by every vtable of the same shape and are not attributable to one slot by static evidence.",
    "one_level_up": "For each reader body this packet records only two counts: raw direct rel32 call/jump byte occurrences in .text whose target is the body start, and .rela.dyn entries whose addend is the body start.  The reader bodies' own callers are outside this packet's question.",
    "prior_packets": "RE-011-evm-permit-routing-115 records two of the seven (reader body, base, stored body) triples as method-table rows -- future body 0x2d087e0 with inner vtable 0x6445868 and inner poll target 0x2a2a0e0 (eth_call), and future body 0x2d062f0 with inner vtable 0x64455c8 and inner poll target 0x2a225c0 (eth_estimateGas) -- without reference sites, use forms, or a completeness census. RE-011-eth-call-path-115, RE-001-node115-channel-repoll-terminal and RE-003-pr-integration-20261103 mention individual body or slot addresses incidentally.  The source packet (RE-005-node115-x5-consumer-callers) counted the seven stored pointers and left their readers as an explicit boundary; no earlier packet enumerates the readers of all seven, pins their reference sites and use forms, or excludes the other reference forms for the slots and bases.",
    "runtime_behaviour": "Which runtime path reaches a given reader, what the per-slot statics name, and the concrete Rust types of the stored and reader bodies are not established by static evidence."
  },
